   expected (asymptotic)        : -2s: 2.38, -1s: 3.36, +0s: 5.05, +1s: 7.81, +2s: 11.80
   no-systematic reference      : CLs UL (n=4, b=3.26) = 6.31
   kappa -> 1.001, r = 6: toy CLs = 0.0489  vs stat-only P(n<=4|9.26)/P(n<=4|3.26) = 0.0608
   -> any continuous global observable breaks the ties between toys with n = n_obs,
      so the toy p-values become ~P(n<n_obs) + P(n=n_obs)/2 ('mid-p') instead of
      P(n<=n_obs): the stat-only discrete CLs limit is conservative.

